# SilikOS — the COMMAND bar: one line where you type an address (app/…, eda/…, win/…, sys/…, a path) and Enter runs it.
# `?QUESTION` asks this system (silik ask, offline): Enter lists the commands that answer, Enter on one puts it in the
# bar as `$ COMMAND` without running it; a line that starts with `$` is a command line, run in a terminal.
# Every entry shows the command line that does the same from a terminal (its "twin"), and what was run goes to the
# session log (~/.local/state/silikos/session.log) so that it can be run again. Bound to Super+Space by the desktop
# defaults (silikos-desktop).
#   silik-command [--query TEXT] [--theme light|dark] [--list TEXT] [--lang en|ca|es]
#   --list prints the matches of TEXT as "address<TAB>twin" and exits (no window: tests, scripts).
# Python 3.9, GTK 3 through python3-gobject; the logic above the "window" line has no GTK in it.
# It stays: Esc, Enter or a click elsewhere hide the window and the process keeps it; the next `silik-command` asks
# that one to show itself (a socket in the user's runtime folder) and ends. A window that is already loaded is on the
# screen in a tenth of the time (docs/STATUS.md). Without a runtime folder it opens and ends as before.
